# NVIDIA GTX 1080 Ti on Fedora 44

**Driver:** proprietary **580xx legacy** from RPM Fusion (`akmod-nvidia-580xx`).
NVIDIA 590+ (Fedora 44 default is 595) dropped Pascal; 580 is the final branch for GTX 10-series.

## Install

```bash
# 1. Full RPM Fusion repos (legacy drivers are NOT in the default "NVIDIA driver" repo)
sudo dnf install \
  https://mirrors.rpmfusion.org/free/fedora/rpmfusion-free-release-$(rpm -E %fedora).noarch.rpm \
  https://mirrors.rpmfusion.org/nonfree/fedora/rpmfusion-nonfree-release-$(rpm -E %fedora).noarch.rpm

# 2. Remove current driver if present, install 580xx
sudo dnf remove xorg-x11-drv-nvidia akmod-nvidia
sudo dnf install akmod-nvidia-580xx xorg-x11-drv-nvidia-580xx xorg-x11-drv-nvidia-580xx-cuda

# 3. Wait for module build, then reboot
modinfo -F version nvidia
sudo reboot
```

## Notes

- **Don't** use `akmod-nvidia` (595, no Pascal) or `akmod-nvidia-open` (no Pascal).
- **Secure Boot:** enroll akmods key, then confirm in MOK screen on reboot:
  ```bash
  sudo kmodgenca -a
  sudo mokutil --import /etc/pki/akmods/certs/public_key.der
  ```
- **Build logs:** `/var/cache/akmods/nvidia-580xx/.last.log`, `/var/log/akmods/akmods.log`
- Nouveau works but is much slower on Pascal (can't reclock).
